{"id":"ff558bae-aa77-4725-80b0-75e6c43f6be8","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"5517c88cd3f220a1#0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/git-service.ts","baseline":{"blob":"936a8535b8a82484dae82ed809b5aa73352b2ed6","start":7752,"end":7764},"shape":{"type":"AssignmentExpression","atoms":["changes","+=","1"]},"context":{"before":"3568d5710aee2910","after":"8c8a916834748a38"}},"payload":{"text":"(a commit is a change to the working tree's status: a walk begun before it, or while it's made, doesn't answer\nwho asks after it — the Source Control view's refresh after its commit kept listing what it had just committed,\nCI's source-control.spec, 2026-11-19. Only the commit's: every `git.changed` counted made a walk more a change,\nand under load rules.spec's run never reached the Debug Console.)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:50:16.422Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:50:16.422Z"}
